  "answer_text": "Great question! Here's everything you need to know about that iconic scene:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf7a Del Boy Falls Through the Bar \u2014 *\"Yuppy Love\"*\n\nThe episode is called **\"Yuppy Love\"**, and it was the first episode of **Series 6** of *Only Fools and Horses*, airing on **8th January 1989** on BBC1, attracting a viewing figure of **13.9 million**.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcfa The Scene\n\nDel Boy (David Jason) accidentally falls through the bar, having attempted to lean up against it while telling Trigger (Roger Lloyd Pack) about what they should do to appear attractive to women. The barman lifts up the bar flap, but Del is unaware of this. He tells Trigger they may be in luck and to \"play it nice and cool\" \u2014 and as he goes to lean on the bar, he falls right over. Trigger looks around wondering where Del is, before Del gets up and tells Trig they are leaving.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfad Behind the Scenes\n\n- The scene was inspired by writer **John Sullivan** watching a man do the exact same thing in a real wine bar, except the man grabbed onto the fixed part of the bar so he didn't fall all the way over. Sullivan found the man's body language trying to recover his cool to be hilarious.\n\n- Sullivan originally wanted a slip, stumble, and tree-like fall, but **David Jason** thought Del should go all the way over \u2014 starting to go sideways, then falling without looking in the direction of the fall, which Jason felt was the key to the scene. There was a hidden crash mat, but it was a difficult shot because it was hard not to look where Jason was falling.\n\n- A rehearsal script that went up for auction revealed that **Trigger wasn't supposed to be in the scene originally**. However, Roger Lloyd Pack happened to be there on the day, and John Sullivan decided he should be included after all.\n\n- Roger Lloyd Pack later revealed that Jason never did the fall during rehearsals, so his reaction was genuine surprise: \"He never did it in rehearsal, so it was a surprise when it came.\"\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfc6 Legacy\n\nDel Boy's fall through the bar has become one of the most celebrated sitcom scenes ever. Jason gets people asking him about that fall all the time, and some never like to talk about anything else, but he's happy to be remembered for something so iconic.\n\nDel falling through the bar was even the inspiration behind a scene 25 years later in the mini episode *Beckham in Peckham* for Sport Relief in March 2014, in which David Beckham falls after leaning on a portable rack that had been moved \u2014 and Del says \"What a plonker.\"",
